  "summary": "whalibmob@5.33.19: static keyword matches without traced installer-harm evidence",
  "details": "static analysis of this package flagged keyword co-occurrences in lib/MediaService.js (fs + http/https + readFileSync + https.request), lib/Registration.js (repeated 'ping' tokens), lib/WebVersion.js (curl, https.get, ps), and lib/socks.js (curl, POST, hostname). These are pattern matches on tokens that routinely appear in benign networking and process-management code and do not, on their own, demonstrate reading installer-side secrets or sending them to an attacker-controlled destination. No concrete attacker-controlled endpoint, credential path (e.g. ~/.aws, ~/.ssh, ~/.npmrc, browser stores), environment-scraping routine, lifecycle-script dropper, or persistence mechanism was identified in the available evidence. The specific behavior and destinations of the flagged code paths are not corroborated.",
